Ladybird sizes the buffer for an active uniform’s or attribute’s name by
the program’s ACTIVE_UNIFORM_MAX_LENGTH or ACTIVE_ATTRIBUTE_MAX_LENGTH.
Blink’s WebGLRenderingContextBase does the same for getActiveAttrib()
and getActiveUniform(), WebKit’s GraphicsContextGLANGLE does it with
ACTIVE_UNIFORM_MAX_LENGTH, and Gecko’s WebGLContext grows its buffer to
that length too. And the test’s output matches Chrome 158, Firefox 151,
and WebKit 26.5, line for line, at 256 characters and at 1024.
